# .graphifyignore — graphify-only exclusion list for the pack repo (BD-225).
# MATCHER: gitignore syntax, as git implements it. `*` does NOT cross `/`; `**`
# IS special; a pattern with no `/` matches a BASENAME at any depth; a leading
# `/` anchors to the repo root; a trailing `/` matches directories only; `!`
# negates; bracket classes `[Aa]` work; last match wins.
# MERGED, NOT EXCLUSIVE: graphify reads .gitignore (including nested ones) AND
# this file. This file is evaluated LAST and wins conflicts, but it can only
# EXCLUDE FURTHER — a `!` here cannot re-include something .gitignore excludes.
# It narrows; it never widens. graphify's built-in always-pruned set
# (graphify-out, node_modules, .git, .venv, build, dist, .next, target, caches)
# applies on top and is NOT re-listed.
# CONSEQUENCE: most entries below are redundant with .gitignore and kept only as
# documentation of intent. The ones doing real work are the archive glob (those
# files are git-TRACKED) and the `.env` family (.gitignore deliberately
# re-includes four fixture .env files; this file excludes them again).
# Index scope = WHOLE REPO minus the exclusions below (BD-225 D6 "start big";
# revisit via BD-234 after burn-in).

# ── Archive dirs AND archive-named files (D1: case-insensitive, any depth) ──
*[Aa][Rr][Cc][Hh][Ii][Vv][Ee]*

# ── Secrets / secrets-adjacent (D2 + privacy posture §8) ──
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
.mcp.json
.claude/settings.local.json

# ── Sub-agent worktree checkouts (mirrors .gitignore) ──
# Isolated per-agent worktrees materialized by sub-agent worktree isolation.
# Each is a FULL second checkout of this repo, so indexing one duplicates every
# node in the graph and corrupts query/affected results. .gitignore carries the
# identical entry and is now merged, so this line is redundant — kept because
# the consequence of losing it is a silently corrupted graph, and a reader
# should not have to consult another file to see that this case is handled.
# Root-anchored by the embedded `/`; directory-only by the trailing `/`.
.claude/worktrees/

# ── Local tracker state (regenerable; no graph value) ──
.pack-tracker/
/tracker.toml

# ── Derived / generated output (pollutes graph with generated symbols) ──
generated/
**/generated/swift/
**/generated/python/

# ── External / not-present reference dir ──
shared-docs/ios26/

# ── OS / editor noise ──
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
._*
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# ── Working-tree-only snapshot ──
scripts/.bd119-pre-refactor-monolith.sh.snapshot

# ── build.sh-generated fixture trees under test-fixtures/ (BD-225) ──
# Mirrors test-fixtures/.gitignore: ignore EVERYTHING under test-fixtures/
# except the committed recipe/manifest files and the static-snapshot dir.
# Future-forward — any NEW generated dir not in the keep-list below is excluded
# automatically (no edit needed): `test-fixtures/*` matches each DIRECT child,
# and excluding a directory excludes its contents, so a single `*` reaches every
# depth without crossing `/` itself. The bare keep-dir line re-includes the
# directory ITSELF, which is what lets its contents be reached at all — a
# negation cannot rescue a file whose parent directory stays excluded. Last
# match wins, so the negations MUST follow the broad exclude. These negations
# are permitted because test-fixtures/.gitignore already admits these same
# paths; this file can only narrow, never re-include past .gitignore.
test-fixtures/*
!test-fixtures/README.md
!test-fixtures/build.sh
!test-fixtures/manifest.txt
!test-fixtures/v11-trinity-marker-prepped
!test-fixtures/v11-trinity-marker-prepped/*
